police reinforcements have been sent to  West Papua to control protests that have  turned violent government buildings  police cars and parts of an airports  have been destroyed the police have been  accused of racism after 43 Paquin  students were arrested for disrespecting  the Indonesian flag on Independence Day  there were reports one flag was set  alight outside a dormitory after being  held for hours the students were  released without charge the government  regrets the burning of the Indonesian  flag the incident is under investigation  the incident was followed by negative  statements which triggered violence  several areas of Papua and West Papua  provinces it is disrupting the nation's  unity the protests came after videos  were shared on social media showing a  school being tear gassed and the  students called monkeys a derogatory  term used against ethnic pop ones for  years Indonesia has blamed indigenous  Pupkin separatists for unrest in the  West Papua new agent but they accused  the government of human rights abuses  during protests on Tuesday 258 inmates  escaped from the prison in the city of  Sarang after it was set on fire the  city's mayor called for calm come on  let's join handing hand together United  in our hearts leave our differences in  maintained togetherness unity and  solidarity between pop ones or non pop  ones Deniz Ian president Joko Widodo  says he's committed to the welfare of  all pup ones but it's not clear if his  words will be enough to calm protesters  they're now calling for a referendum on  independence Sora hi dad and Jazeera
 

